  "scope": [
    "Define a project-owned matched evaluation contract that compares model and reasoning profiles only within the same exact task shape and quality rubric.",
    "Produce deterministic, explainable advisory recommendations from qualified matched evaluations while preserving requested and effective model evidence.",
    "Expose confidence, evidence coverage, rejection reasons, staleness, and fallback behavior through usage report and preflight without executing a model switch.",
    "Keep raw prompts and hidden reasoning out of evaluation records; keep observations project-local and leave automatic routing, cross-project learning, adaptive policy mutation, provider spend, and live generation out of scope."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "A versioned schema validates matched evaluation records, quality measures, task-shape identity, candidate profiles, revisions, and provenance; missing, mixed, stale, or incomparable evidence fails closed.",
    "A deterministic advisory engine recommends a profile only when the project policy's configured quality and statistical decision contract is satisfied; otherwise it reports exact blockers and keeps the Seed Policy.",
    "The recommendation weighs quality before Token use and reports Tokens, latency, rework, and human intervention without claiming causal savings from unmatched observations.",
    "Usage report, preflight, tests, and documentation prove that execution_status remains not-implemented, automatic_routing remains false, and no model switch or provider call occurs.",
    "English, Japanese, and Traditional Chinese README claims remain structurally aligned and describe only the shipped observation and advisory boundary."
  ],
